From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] drm/msm/a6xx: fix inverted PDC sleep guard

GMU_STATUS_FW_START records that firmware has initialized the registers
needed for the PDC sleep sequence. Return when that flag is absent, not
when it is present.

The inverted guard skips normal GPU RSC shutdown after every firmware
start and permits it before initialization or on a repeated stop. Fix the
shared helper used by normal shutdown, force-off and resume error cleanup.

The original Book4 module contains this inverted branch. DDR residency
remains at 4224 MHz during suspend despite removal of the Linux GPU ICC
vote. With this correction, boot and deep-suspend resume succeed and DDR
spends essentially all suspension at 547 MHz instead. Linux sleep votes
are unchanged. Full SoC collapse and suspend wattage remain unresolved.

Fixes: f248d5d5159a ("drm/msm/a6xx: Fix PDC sleep sequence")
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index d9d10f5a7..06d4cfe25 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@ static void a6xx_rpmh_stop(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
